adjoin.body_md:
Returns the union of the set *a* with `{x}`.


`adjoin` complains if *a* is not a literal set.


`adjoin(x, a)` and `union(set(x), a)`
are equivalent;
however, `adjoin` may be somewhat faster than `union`.


See also `disjoin`.


Examples:







```maxima
maxima

(%i1) adjoin (c, {a, b});
(%o1)                       {a, b, c}


(%i2) adjoin (a, {a, b});
(%o2)                        {a, b}
```

See also: `disjoin`.

