bffac.body_md:
Bigfloat version of the factorial (shifted gamma)
function.  The second argument is how many digits to retain and return,
it’s a good idea to request a couple of extra.








```maxima
maxima

(%i1) bffac(1/2,16);
(%o1)                 8.862269254527584b-1


(%i2) (1/2)!,numer;
(%o2)                   0.886226925452758


(%i3) bffac(1/2,32);
(%o3)          8.862269254527580136490837416707b-1
```

bfzeta.body_md:
Returns the Riemann zeta function for the argument *s*.
The return value is a big float (bfloat);
*n* is the number of digits in the return value.

bigfloat_bits.body_md:
Returns the number of bits of precision in a bigfloat number.  This
value depends, of course, on the value of `fpprec`. 









```maxima
(%i1) fpprec:16;
(%o1)                                 16
(%i2) bigfloat_bits();
(%o2)                                 56
(%i3) fpprec:32;
(%o3)                                 32
(%i4) bigfloat_bits();
(%o4)                                 109
```

See also: `fpprec`.

bindtest.body_md:
The command `declare(x, bindtest)` tells Maxima to trigger an error
when the symbol *x* is evaluated unbound.









evaluation: unbound variable aa
 – an error. To debug this try: debugmode(true);


```maxima
maxima

